aims-os-everything (2.1+1) trixie; urgency=medium

  * Demote aims-os-branding from Depends to Recommends. The apt repo
    does not carry aims-os-branding (its payload needs the ISO render
    pipeline; apt-repo/build-debs.sh skips it), so the hard dependency
    made this metapackage uninstallable on a vanilla Debian Trixie.
    ISO installs already have branding in place; vanilla installs now
    get every other layer and apt merely warns about the recommend.

 -- AIMS Senegal IT <hakim@aims-senegal.org>  Wed, 29 Jul 2026 15:10:00 +0000

aims-os-everything (2.1) trixie; urgency=medium

  * Initial release. Convenience metapackage that pulls every AIMS OS
    layer so existing v2.0 users can keep the full install in one apt
    command after upgrading to v2.1's slim base.

